# Shared server-side configuration for session chat, ghost text, and Azure voice.
# Copy to .env in the repository root and replace these placeholders.
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://YOUR-RESOURCE.openai.azure.com/openai/v1
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=YOUR-KEY
DEPLOYMENT_NAME=YOUR-DEPLOYMENT

# Only needed when the endpoint is a legacy resource root (without /openai/v1):
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION=2025-04-01-preview

# Optional Azure Realtime voice: uncomment and configure all three independently.
# Use a Realtime deployment, not DEPLOYMENT_NAME; the endpoint has no /openai/v1 path.
# Or export SPEC_AZURE_REALTIME_ENV_FILE=/absolute/path/to/private-voice.env
# in the local Rust server's launch environment, not in this dotenv file.
# That file replaces this shared file for Azure voice only; text settings stay unchanged.
# If unset, voice uses SPEC_AI_ENV_FILE or the nearest .env. Process voice exports
# override file values, even when empty. Restart the server and reload the browser.
# Invalid Azure voice config disables only Azure voice with a sanitized warning;
# shared text config errors still fail startup. Never put secrets in the browser.
# AZURE_OPENAI_REALTIME_ENDPOINT=https://YOUR-RESOURCE.openai.azure.com
# AZURE_OPENAI_REALTIME_API_KEY=YOUR-REALTIME-KEY
# AZURE_OPENAI_REALTIME_DEPLOYMENT=YOUR-REALTIME-DEPLOYMENT

# Skills marketplace: leave ALL marketplace variables unset for example-only demo.
# Any partial configuration fails startup; it never silently falls back to demo.
# Server only. Never place these values in frontend/VITE variables or return URLs.
# Configure GitHub + PayPal together, then restart. See docs/SKILLS_MARKETPLACE.md.
# SPEC_SKILLS_GITHUB_TOKEN=github-fine-grained-token-with-contents-read
# SPEC_SKILLS_GITHUB_REPO=YOUR-OWNER/YOUR-PRIVATE-SKILLS-REPO
# SPEC_SKILLS_GITHUB_REF=main
# SPEC_PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=YOUR-SANDBOX-APP-CLIENT-ID
# SPEC_PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=YOUR-SANDBOX-APP-SECRET
# SPEC_PAYPAL_MERCHANT_ID=YOUR-SANDBOX-BUSINESS-MERCHANT-ID
# SPEC_PAYPAL_RETURN_URL=https://YOUR-SPEC-HOST/
# SPEC_PAYPAL_MODE=sandbox
# sandbox is the configured default; real payments require explicit live + live credentials.
# Return URL must be HTTPS with no credentials, query or fragment (never #token=...).
